ecil 1.2 features=0x0000000a
; C++ (ECIL 1.2, slice S2): the layouts of classes with virtual bases: empty
; and nearly empty virtual bases, a virtual base with a tail that is reused, a
; diamond with a shared non-polymorphic virtual base, a primary virtual base
; (VN2 : virtual N), virtual bases next to bit-fields.  The program prints
; sizes, alignments and the offsets of members and of base subobjects (through
; static_cast): the output is g++'s (and clang's) for the same source.
; RUN: %ecil-asm %s -o %t.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=obj -o %t.o %t.ecil
; RUN: g++ %t.o -o %t.exe
; RUN: %t.exe | %FileCheck %s --match-full-lines
; CHECK: sizes 16 16 8 16 16 40 16 24 16 16 16 16 8 8
; CHECK-NEXT: VE 8 0
; CHECK-NEXT: VN 8 0
; CHECK-NEXT: VN2 0
; CHECK-NEXT: VP 8 12
; CHECK-NEXT: D1 32 8 24 16 36
; CHECK-NEXT: D1v 5 6 7 8
; CHECK-NEXT: VB 8 0 12
; CHECK-NEXT: DB 0 8 0 20
; CHECK-NEXT: VT 8 9
; CHECK-NEXT: Z0 8
; CHECK-NEXT: W1 8 0 12 4 9
; CHECK-NEXT: BF 3 -15 120 11 12

